# Quality gates

Before claiming a slice done, `npm run check` must pass (typecheck + Biome + Vitest).

## Rules changes

- Game rules live in `src/games/*/game.ts`.
- Add or update a failing Vitest first, then implement until green.
- Prefer driving moves through boardgame.io `Client` (or exported pure helpers) — do not reimplement rules in tests.

## UI / flow changes

- Host, join, or vs-bot path changes need a Playwright smoke update or addition under `e2e/` when the path is user-facing.
- Prefer stable `data-testid` hooks over CSS class selectors.

## Do not

- Skip git hooks (`--no-verify`) to land green.
- Weaken `check` / CI to hide failures.
- Claim done on typecheck alone when rules or flows changed.

## Commands

- Fast loop: `npm run check`
- Full CI locally: `npm run ci` (requires build + Playwright browsers)
